\ A wrong twin: exists h, k makes ⟨h, k, ?_⟩, its rest against b = a (467,
\ at the exists word, where the macro puts it).
\ (plan row TB2, tactic batch 3c; batch-f-wrong.lean)
\ Lean: theorem w_exists_many (a b : Nat) (h : a = b) (k : b = a) : a = b ∧ b = a := by
\         exists h, k
theorem w_exists_many
  Nat explicit: a  Nat explicit: b
  a b = explicit: h  b a = explicit: k
  a b = b a = ∧
:= by
  by-exists[ ' h ' k ]
end w_exists_many
